# MANDATORY: TRANSOVO UI Design Guide

**Scope:** All repository work — pages, APIs, `src/lib/`, jobs, and any customer-facing behavior. Read the full source doc before implementing.

**Source of truth:** `docs/TRANSOVO-UI-DESIGN-GUIDE.md`  
**Authority:** Level 1 — domain definitions, terminology, product experience principles.

## Hard requirement

Before creating or editing any customer-facing UI, you **MUST** read the full guide and comply. This is not optional reference material.

## Non-negotiables

- Use **one application shell** — do not reinvent chrome per page.
- Use **canonical Transovo terminology** — no duplicate names for the same object.
- Every feature has **one canonical nav home**; contextual links OK, duplicate architecture not OK.
- Prefer **recognition over recall**; expose status and next actions clearly.
- **Mutually exclusive** choices use radio/select patterns, not ambiguous toggles.
- Operational pages show **real data states** — never placeholder-only success UI.
- Settings that appear in UI must **map to runtime behavior**.

## When this applies

All routes under `src/app/`, `src/components/`, `src/kimi-ui/`, and shared presentation layers.

## On conflict

`docs/TRANSOVO-PRODUCT-DESIGN-UX-GOVERNANCE.md` wins. Read it first.
